      "host": "point-right",
      "hasAudio": true
    },
    {
      "scene": 8,
      "narration": "Lý Thái Tổ nổi bật ở khả năng xây dựng một quốc gia ổn định sau thời kỳ loạn lạc.",
      "image": {
        "kind": "ai",
        "characters": [
          "ly-thai-to"
        ],
        "identity": "full",
        "prompt": "Reviewing the construction of a stable new capital, gesturing calmly toward planners, builders and officials organizing roads, storehouses and defensive walls. Setting: early-11th-century Thăng Long in Đại Việt beside the Red River, with low brick ramparts, round-arched passages, timber halls on stout posts and dark unglazed tiles. Vietnamese workers and soldiers have East-Asian faces and wear plain early-Lý tunics, head cloths and simple guard equipment. The scene should feel practical, orderly and hopeful, with clear evidence of administration replacing disorder. No Chinese imperial megacity, no Nguyễn-dynasty costume, no European masonry."
